# U8, intranode direct access: bale's tensor conveyor, on-node (local) porter.
# The sender copies a full buffer straight into the peer's receive area and
# stores a signal word there, both through pointers from shmem_ptr. The
# receiver polls its signal words with plain atomic loads (putport.c:109) and,
# once it has used the buffer, acknowledges with an ordinary one-word put.
#
# Against §8.6: the local send path has no fence (putport.c:328-348); only the
# RMA porter fences (:261). And the acknowledgement stays RMA even on-node.
#
# Setup, outside this trace: shmem_ptr on each on-node peer's receive buffers
# and signal array (putport.c:309,311), once per porter setup (:302-317).
trace     U8-bale-convey-local
workload  U8
source    bale 1b8f673b56645b2bd74a8af6213462bbc9d559fe
loop      src/bale_classic/convey/putport.c:328-348  one buffer sent to an on-node PE, and its acknowledgement (:175-199)
threads   1
build     MPP_USE_SHMEM and CONVEY_INTRANODE, which needs HAVE_SHMEM_PTR and lock-free 64-bit atomics (common.h:23-25); the tensor conveyor gives its on-node porters porter_opt_LOCAL (tensor.c:466-467, putport.c:522,579)
param     BUF  data   # bytes in the buffer, at most the porter's buffer size

# The destination is one of the PEs on this node (tensor.c:462-463), chosen by
# where the buffered items are going: random within the node.
role sender  the PE whose buffer is full
  direct  store  1  BUF  random  -  src/bale_classic/convey/putport.c:339  # memcpy into the peer's receive buffer
  direct  store  8  1    random  -  src/bale_classic/convey/putport.c:346  # atomic store of the signal word
end
role receiver  the on-node PE that received it, after using the buffer
  call  shmem_longlong_p  8  1  random  default  src/bale_classic/convey/putport.c:194  # consumed[slot] on the sender
end
